# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values there. `.env` is
# gitignored and never committed -- only variable *names* belong in version
# control, never values.
#
# .env is loaded automatically by the repo-root conftest.py before any test
# runs (python-dotenv) -- nothing else in graphtrace reads it directly.
#
# judge.model in graphtrace.yaml is a plain litellm model string -- litellm
# itself reads the one matching provider key below straight from the
# environment, based on that string's prefix. Only fill in the one you're
# actually going to use; the others can stay commented out or absent.
# (Confirmed by hand: judge/client.py never reads an env var itself -- it
# just calls litellm.completion(model=..., ...) and lets litellm resolve
# the provider key on its own. An earlier draft of this file documented a
# GRAPHTRACE_JUDGE_API_KEY variable that nothing in the codebase ever read --
# a real bug, fixed here rather than left to confuse the first real setup.)

# Groq (fast/cheap inference for open models -- NOT the same company as
# Grok/xAI, confusingly similar name) -- judge.model: groq/openai/gpt-oss-120b
# or groq/qwen/qwen3.8-27b (confirmed real model names via litellm's own
# model_list, not guessed; same models kbguard's own judge config uses).
GROQ_API_KEY=

# xAI / Grok -- judge.model: xai/grok-4.5 (or whatever's current on x.ai's console)
#XAI_API_KEY=

# OpenAI -- judge.model: gpt-4o-mini
#OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic -- judge.model: anthropic/claude-3-5-sonnet-...
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
